  "title": "P-ary m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from Martínez-Cagigal et al. (2023)",
  "description": "EEG dataset of code-modulated visual evoked potentials (c-VEP) brain-computer interface recordings using non-binary (p-ary) m-sequences. Sixteen healthy participants were recorded with 16 EEG channels at 256 Hz. Each participant completed five conditions, each with eight runs (six for training, two for testing), and the stimulus classes are labeled with 11 event codes. The dataset supports research on more comfortable c-VEP-based BCI stimulation.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 16 channels at 256 Hz (standard_1005 montage, 50 Hz line frequency). Each of five conditions was stored as a separate session to match the MOABB structure, with eight runs per session (six for training and two for testing). Visual stimuli were presented using p-ary m-sequences.",
